.git
.pytest_cache
.qodo
.claude
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.db
*.sqlite
# data/ is deliberately NOT excluded wholesale. A blanket `data/` rule shipped
# an image with an empty collections page: data/collections/*.json is curated
# content that must be in the image, and a negation exception (`!data/...`)
# depends on Docker's nested-path semantics, which are easy to get subtly wrong
# and cannot be tested without a Docker daemon.
#
# The thing that actually needs excluding is the 2.7GB metadata sidecar, which
# the image fetches at build time rather than copying from the host. The
# *.sqlite and *.db rules above already cover it; these are explicit for
# anyone reading this file in isolation.
data/*.sqlite
data/*.db
*.ipynb
pdf_images/
notebooks/
*.pdf
.env
